    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2790e2fd-fe0e-53ef-a1f2-d41cf3f3895b",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -15 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $-3$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | $4$ | $4$ |  |\n|  |  | $-15$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-1}} |  |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\cdot C \\\\  & =C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -15 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
